            <ArticleTitle>[Transluminal coronary dilatation].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>2065-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Percutaneous transluminal coronary angioplasty (PTCA) represents in patients with single-vessel disease the treatment of choice. Under adequate precautions the method can be performed with reasonable risk outside of a hospital with cardiac surgical operating rooms.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
